From d143b543cd843bdb1bfe9e7f89af39827fcee673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Fran=C3=A7ois=20Roux?= <info@humanlearning.ch>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:08:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Surface Pro 12 camera series, backported
 from CyberMyth OS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The camera enablement series by Mias van Klei, as carried by CyberMyth OS for its
7.2.3 kernel (github.com/CyberMyth-OS/Surface-Pro-12, kernel/sp12-v7.2-rc7.patch).
Three parts, all of which apply to next-20260626 without a single conflict:

  drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-mipi-csi2*   929 lines, three new files
  drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/*        443 lines across seven files
  drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c, ov02c10.c     976 lines; both drivers already
                                             existed in this tree, merely unbuilt

Enabled as modules: PHY_QCOM_MIPI_CSI2, VIDEO_OV13858, VIDEO_OV02C10, alongside
the VIDEO_QCOM_CAMSS that was already m. All four build clean against the running
kernel and are installed.

⚠️ This is the driver half only. Our device tree carries the camera clock
controller but no camss, cci, csiphy or sensor node, so nothing binds yet. The
nodes have to be grafted from the CyberMyth device tree, which is the remaining
work.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: François Roux <info@humanlearning.ch>
